2 TITL Cemetery Hartshorn Oklahoma Robinson family plot._6036
1 _OID 1f165f2a-9816-4bc9-815e-3c191bb892a3
1 PLAC Elmwood Cemetery, Harsthorn, Oklahoma Robinson family plot
1 _DSCR Sent to me by Barbara Ledbetter, who got this from our relatives in Oklahoma, (Jane Impson Robinson is my great Grandmother) it shows placements of the graves of the Robinson family
1 _META <metadataxml><acountry></acountry><branch></branch><cemetery></cemetery><country></country><directions></directions><ingredients></ingredients><institution></institution><job></job><ocountry></ocountry><school></school><transcription>This is a char
2 CONC t of the Robinson cemetery plots.  
2 CONT 
2 CONT C.H. (Charles Hamilton) Robinson was the son of Charles &amp; Rose Robinson.  Jane &amp; John Robinson’s grandson.    He died at 19 in a swimming accident.
2 CONT 
2 CONT Jane Impson Robinson 
2 CONT Broke her hip &amp; later died of a heart attack.
2 CONT 
2 CONT Wesley Killebrew son of Esther &amp; Bill Killebrew. Grandson of Jane &amp; John Robinson.  He fell into a bucket of hot lye water Esther was using to mop her floors.
2 CONT 
2 CONT Baby Girl Killebrew daughter of Bill &amp; Esther Killebrew died at birth.
2 CONT 
2 CONT Laura Robinson wife of Walter Robinson.  Walter was stepson of Jane Robinson.  John Robinson’s son by first wife.
2 CONT 
2 CONT Walter Robinson stepson of Jane Robinson.  Son of John Robinson by first wife.  Died in work related accident.  
2 CONT 
2 CONT Rose Hamilton Robinson daughter-in-law to Jane Robinson.  Wife of Charles Robinson. Mother of C.H. (Charles Hamilton).   Died of tuberculosis.
2 CONT 
2 CONT Charles “Charlie” Robinson son of Jane &amp; John Robinson.  Father of C.H. Robinson.  Died of tuberculosis.
2 CONT 
2 CONT Theresa  “Tess” Robinson daughter of Jane &amp; John Robinson.  Engaged to a Mr. Davidson. Committed suicide.  She drank lye.
2 CONT 
2 CONT John Robinson husband of Jane Robinson.</transcription><personas><persona><pname></pname><bdate></bdate><bplace></bplace><ddate></ddate><dplace></dplace></persona></personas></metadataxml>
