2 CONC t George&amp;rsquo;s Creek about eight miles, where a messenger came with letters from my son, who was just returned from his people at the Cherokees, and lay sick at the mouth of Conegocheague. But as I found myself entered again on public busines
2 CONC s, and Major Washington and all the company unwilling I should return I wrote and sent medicines to my son, and so continued my journey, and encamped at a big hill in the forks of Youghiogany, about eighteen miles.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line></co
2 CONC ntent></metadataxml>
