2 CONC d 21 Aug 1741 in Baltimore Co,MD. He married Zipporah Murray on 07 Dec 1704 in Friends Meeting House,Baltimore,MD, daughter of James Murray and Jemina Morgan.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Richard was abt. 7 yrs. old when his father died and abt. 11 yrs. ol
2 CONC d when his mother died. He married 12/7/1704, at the Quaker Meeting House, Baltimore Co., MD. He resided at Gist&apos;s Rest and later moved to Brother&apos;s Good Will. He was captain of the militia, planter, and County Justice and Commissioner.&l
2 CONC t;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;He was the surveyor of the Town of Baltimore.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Died 2: 28 Aug 1741, Baltimore Co, MD.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Children of Richard Gist and Zipporah Murray are:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt; Captain Nathaniel Gist, b. 1707, MD
2 CONC , d. 07 Oct 1770, Sevier,Tennessee.&lt;br&gt; Christopher Gist, b. 1705, St. Paul&apos;s, Baltimore, d. 25 Jul 1759, Winchester,VA. [m. Sarah Howard]&lt;br&gt; Edith Gist, b. 1709, Baltimore Co.,MD, d. Aft. 1770, Baltimore Co.,MD. [m. Vaughan]&lt;b
