2 TITL Marriage Certificate John W. Robinson and Jane Impson PAGE 1
1 _OID f85f8858-7f3c-45e4-a6dd-0f700a042908
1 DATE 03 Jan 1883
1 PLAC Jacks Fork County
1 _DSCR Page one of Marriage cert 
2 CONT A.O. Brown County Judge 
2 CONT Jacks Fork County 
2 CONT www.ancestry.com/mediaui-viewer/tree/28102913/person
1 _META <metadataxml><transcription>The Choctaw Nation
2 CONT 
2 CONT To all to whom these precincts shall come Guessing?: Know ye: that I, A.O. Brown County probate Judge of Jacks Fork County Choctaw Nation, do hereby this day Grant a License unto J. W. Robetson (Robinson) a citizen of the United States, who desirin
2 CONC g to marry a Choctaw woman and is a resident of the aforesaid county and Nation and has presented to me signers with Four respectable Choctaw citizens by blood who states that they have known him to be of good moral character.  Twelve months immedi
2 CONC ately preceding the signing of this certificate and has also taken the Oath as are required by law, Given under my hand and Seal this 3 day of Jan. 1883.
2 CONT A.O. V. Brown County &amp; Pro. Judge
2 CONT Jacks Fork County Ok.
2 CONT 
2 CONT This is to certify that I have this day performed as administrator this marriage ceremony between J. W. Robertson (Robinson) and Miss Janey (Jane Jensie) Impson according to law.
2 CONT A.O. Brown County Judge Jacks Fork Co. OK. 
2 CONT This Jan 10 A.D. 1883
2 CONT Itta haloth Holliso illappot Feb 16th 1883 felma sabok fora cha Hollisso chito mamisht ai attali .
2 CONT (choctaw language at end of document.) goes then to page 2</transcription></metadataxml>
